{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"3bbbddee-21cf-4853-9c6f-5efda0229a8d","runId":"c9957232-12d8-4189-81a8-05e3c2503850","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:ae26b81dc3ae071dbc3b38dca241f2444a979b94e4f9858eb41312129b8efb34","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a0433f-cfac-7482-a691-fbdbfc46f10d","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T12:47:15.782Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":["Current source rejects malformed issue numbers before path interpolation.","The finding is stale relative to the frozen integration base.","Focused test coverage remains justified and in scope."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Verdict | **Invalid** |\n| Confidence | **High** |\n| Severity | **Medium** |\n| Task Type | `security regression validation` |\n\n### What Was Claimed\n\n`GitHubIssueProjector.setWorkflowLabel` was reported to interpolate an unvalidated `issueNumber` into GitHub API paths, allowing malformed runtime values to influence the transport route.\n\n### What We Found\n\nThe frozen `staging` base already rejects non-positive and non-safe-integer values in `setWorkflowLabel`. Its shared `#replaceWorkflowLabel` implementation independently calls `requireIssueNumber(issueNumber)` before constructing either the issue or labels path. The reported current defect is therefore not reproducible at `7817370b07c7e3d172f4971771e822aab548431a`.\n\nFocused regression coverage for hostile runtime values is absent, so this run will add test-only coverage to preserve the existing safety behavior.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe source finding describes an earlier reviewed head (`a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`) that no longer matches the integration branch. The current implementation has restored validation, but no focused test pins rejection before transport access.\n\n### Affected Files\n\n| Path | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| `src/adapters/github-projection.ts` | Current implementation contains both the public guard and a shared pre-interpolation guard. |\n| `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` | Existing workflow-label tests cover valid transitions but not malformed issue numbers. |\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `setWorkflowLabel` checks `Number.isSafeInteger(issueNumber)` and requires a value of at least 1.\n- `#replaceWorkflowLabel` calls `requireIssueNumber(issueNumber)` before constructing `${this.#apiRoot}/issues/${issueNumber}`.\n- No test currently asserts rejection of malformed runtime issue numbers or absence of transport calls.\n\n### History Findings\n\n- Issue #209 was derived from security finding `security-001` on PR #199 at reviewed head `a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`.\n- The frozen integration base differs from that reviewed head and already contains the guard.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nRetain the current implementation and add a focused adapter regression test proving malformed runtime issue numbers are rejected before any GitHub transport request. Do not expand into unrelated projection behavior.\n\n### Related Issues\n\n- Source review finding: issue `#209`, derived from PR `#199`.\n\n### Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The remaining work is a single focused test change.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- [x] Validate the finding against the current integration branch.\n- [x] Confirm the shared implementation validates before interpolation.\n- [ ] Add focused regression coverage for malformed runtime issue numbers.\n- [ ] Re-review the exact remediation head.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->","outputArtifactHash":"sha256:investigate-209-current-guard"}}
