{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"708d2132-35ee-44b2-a1a1-ac125a0864c3","runId":"c9957232-12d8-4189-81a8-05e3c2503850","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":20,"previousEventHash":"sha256:25666922ae40aea1f866ecb4a128e160823a67db75d4e2a5d165f0748d1599b0","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a0433f-cfac-7482-a691-fbdbfc46f10d","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T12:49:28.238Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":["Contract is limited to one test file.","Acceptance criteria map directly to investigation checks.","No product or authority decision is required."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:CONTRACT -->\n## Builder Contract\n\n### Objective\n\nAdd focused regression coverage proving `GitHubIssueProjector.setWorkflowLabel` rejects malformed runtime issue numbers before issuing a GitHub transport request.\n\n### Allowed Paths\n\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts`\n\n### Forbidden Changes\n\n- Production behavior in `src/`.\n- Workflow authority, schemas, labels, API routes, or projection semantics.\n- Dependency, configuration, or documentation changes.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- Valid positive safe-integer issue numbers retain existing behavior.\n- Invalid issue numbers never reach the transport.\n- The canonical `TypeError` message remains `Issue number must be positive.`.\n- Tests contain no credentials or external network access.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- A focused regression test for malformed issue-number values.\n- Passing required `check` verification.\n- Fresh correctness and security review of the committed head.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Representative path-like strings, fractional numbers, non-positive values, and unsafe integers reject with `TypeError`.\n- [ ] No transport request occurs for any invalid value.\n- [ ] `npm run check` passes through the bound `check` command.\n- [ ] The frozen committed head passes the required reviewer panel.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT -->\n## Implementation Context\n\n### History\n\nIssue #209 originated from PR #199 security finding `security-001` at head `a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`. The frozen integration base already has both a public guard and shared pre-interpolation validation.\n\n### Callers And Data Flow\n\n`setWorkflowLabel(issueNumber, workflowLabel)` validates the workflow label and delegates to `#replaceWorkflowLabel`. The shared method validates `issueNumber` before composing the issue and labels endpoints, then accesses the injected `GitHubTransport`.\n\n### CI Surface\n\nThe tracked required check is `npm run check`, which runs TypeScript typechecking and the complete Node test suite.\n\n### Prior Findings\n\nThe source security finding is stale against the current integration base. Its durable concern remains valid as a regression boundary, and no focused test currently exercises runtime type violations.\n\n### Hazards\n\n- TypeScript annotations alone do not protect JavaScript or deserialized callers.\n- A test that only checks rejection but not transport access could miss late validation.\n- Production edits would exceed the validated remaining scope.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT:COMPLETE -->\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT -->\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Add a test transport that records or fails on any request.\n2. Exercise representative malformed runtime values through `setWorkflowLabel`, using an explicit unsafe cast only at the test boundary.\n3. Assert the canonical `TypeError` for every value and assert zero transport requests.\n4. Run the bound `check` command and commit the test-only change.\n5. Prepare the PR and run the required fresh correctness and security panel at the frozen head.\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT:COMPLETE -->","outputArtifactHash":"sha256:plan-209-test-only"}}
